ors and professors that investigates the ecology, geology and sustainability of the region. Activities will include tours of forests and wetlands, visits to the Leopold Center and the International Crane Foundation, and a geological hike. Lodging is at Durward's Glen Retreat and Conference Center. Attendance at weekly class meetings before and after the trip required. The very low course fee is thanks to the generous financial support from the Buckley Student Fund for ESES students, which is covering the majority of the cost. The trip dates are October 2-4. Grading will be S/U. Attendance at weekly class meetings before and after the trip required."}]},{"id":"ESE 311","subject":"ESE","number":"311","title":"Environmental Issues Today","creditHours":"3 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"79374","code":"A","typeCode":"LCD","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"1","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Lecture-Discussion","typeCode":"LCD","days":["T","R"],"start":570,"end":650,"location":"11 Psychology Building","instructors":["Meghani, N"]}],"restrictions":[],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"ESE 320","subject":"ESE","number":"320","title":"Water Planet, Water Crisis","creditHours":"3 hours","minHours":3,"genEd":[],"degreeAttributes":"","scheduleNote":"","info":"Same as GEOL 370 and GGIS 370.","linkedByLetter":false,"sections":[{"crn":"64423","code":"A","typeCode":"ONL","group":"lecture","status":"unknown","statusText":"","partOfTerm":"B","dateRange":"","meetings":[{"typeName":"Online","typeCode":"ONL","days":[],"start":null,"end":null,"location":"n.a.","instructors":["Cole, T"]}],"restrictions":["Restricted to Earth, Soc, Env Sustainability major(s)."],"coRequest":null,"specialApproval":null,"sectionText":null}]},{"id":"ESE 360","subject":"ESE","number":"360","title":"Environmental Writing","creditHours":"3 hours","m